const FAQ_ITEMS = [
  { q: 'What is TranslateNow?', a: 'TranslateNow is an AI-powered translation app for iOS that supports 135+ languages with voice cloning, AR translation, document translation, camera OCR, a keyboard extension, AI writing tools, and offline mode. It also integrates with Siri Shortcuts, Home Screen widgets, Control Center, Live Activities, Dynamic Island, Spotlight search, and the iOS 18.4+ system translator API. Developed by Coachie AI.' },
  { q: 'How does voice cloning work in TranslateNow?', a: 'Voice cloning lets you record a 10-second voice sample that ElevenLabs uses to create an AI replica of your voice speaking in any of 135+ languages. You can also upload an audio file instead of recording. Choose male or female voice gender, adjust playback speed from 0.5x to 2x, and hear translations in your own voice with natural intonation. Voice cloning is a Pro feature.' },
  { q: 'What is AR Real-Time Translation?', a: 'AR Translation uses ARKit to detect text through your iPhone camera and overlays 3D floating glassmorphism translation cards anchored in real-world space via SceneKit. Point your camera at signs, menus, or documents — translations appear floating in 3D space. Tap any card to copy text, hear TTS pronunciation, or feel haptic feedback. Translations persist as you move your camera.' },
  { q: 'Can TranslateNow translate PDF, Word, and text documents?', a: 'Yes, TranslateNow translates PDF, DOCX, TXT, and photo documents with layout preservation. The parser extracts every text block, GPT-4o translates each one, and the reconstruction engine rebuilds the document keeping original formatting, fonts, and layout intact. Full RTL support is included for Arabic, Hebrew, and Urdu.' },
  { q: 'Can I translate offline without internet on iPhone?', a: 'Yes, 59 languages are available for fully offline, on-device translation via Google ML Kit. Download language packs once over WiFi (5-50 MB each), then translate anywhere without internet. Zero data is transmitted — all processing stays on your iPhone.' },
  { q: 'How does the keyboard translator work?', a: 'The keyboard translator is a built-in iOS keyboard extension that works inside every app with a text field — iMessage, WhatsApp, Instagram, Telegram, LinkedIn, Gmail, Slack, and more. Type in your language, and the keyboard translates and sends in the target language without switching apps.' },
  { q: 'What AI writing tools are included?', a: 'TranslateNow includes 5 AI writing tools that modify text before translation: Grammar (auto-fix spelling and errors), Tone (Friendly, Professional, Funny, Flirty, Simplified), Length (Concise at 40-60% or Extended at 150-200%), Format (Summary, Key Points, Bullet List), and Style (Academic, Creative, Poetic, Persuasive). No other translator app has built-in writing tools.' },
  { q: 'Does TranslateNow support Siri, Widgets, Control Center, and Live Activities?', a: 'Yes, TranslateNow has deep iOS integration. It includes 5 Siri Shortcuts, 3 Home Screen widget types (Quick Translate, Recent Translations, Word of the Day), 3 iOS 18 Control Center controls (Camera, Voice, Text), Live Activities on Lock Screen and Dynamic Island during active sessions, and Spotlight search indexing for your 50 most recent translations.' },
  { q: "Can I set TranslateNow as my iPhone's default translator?", a: "Yes, on iOS 18.4 and later, TranslateNow registers as a system translation provider. When you select text in Safari, Mail, or Messages and tap 'Translate' from the context menu, the translation routes through TranslateNow instead of Apple's built-in translator." },
  { q: 'How much does TranslateNow cost?', a: 'TranslateNow is free to download with basic translation features. Premium plans are: Weekly at $9.99/week (includes a 3-day free trial) and Monthly at $29.99/month (best value, save 25%). Both plans unlock voice cloning, AI writing tools, document translation, AR translation, and all premium features. Cancel anytime via Apple subscription management.' },
  { q: 'What makes TranslateNow better than Google Translate and DeepL?', a: "TranslateNow has 22 features that neither Google Translate nor DeepL offer. These include AI voice cloning, AR real-time translation with ARKit, 5 built-in writing tools, a keyboard translator for any app, document translation with layout reconstruction, system default translator (iOS 18.4+), Siri Shortcuts, 3 Home Screen widgets, Control Center controls, Live Activities with Dynamic Island, conversation recording as .m4a, AI context with examples and synonyms, transliteration for non-Latin scripts, 9 translation tones, 7 neural AI voices, and playback speed control." },
  { q: 'Does TranslateNow work in WhatsApp, iMessage, and Instagram?', a: 'Yes. The built-in keyboard extension works in any iOS app with a text field — WhatsApp, iMessage, Instagram, Telegram, LinkedIn, Gmail, Slack, and all others. Enable it in Settings → General → Keyboard → Keyboards → Add New Keyboard → TranslateNow.' },
  { q: 'How many languages does TranslateNow support?', a: 'TranslateNow supports 135+ languages for cloud translation via GPT-4o, 59 languages for offline on-device translation via Google ML Kit, and the app interface is localized in 30 languages including Hindi, Spanish, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Chinese, Arabic, and Hebrew.' },
  { q: 'Is TranslateNow safe for private translations?', a: 'In offline mode, all translation processing happens entirely on your iPhone via ML Kit with zero data transmitted. For cloud features, text is processed through OpenAI and ElevenLabs APIs with standard encryption. No translation data is stored on Coachie AI servers.' },
  // ═══ NEW: "How to" queries for AEO/voice search ═══
  { q: 'How to translate WhatsApp messages on iPhone?', a: 'To translate WhatsApp messages on iPhone, enable the TranslateNow keyboard extension in Settings → General → Keyboard → Keyboards → Add New Keyboard → TranslateNow. Then open WhatsApp, tap the globe icon on your keyboard to switch to TranslateNow, type your message in your language, and it automatically translates before sending. Works with any language pair from 135+ supported languages.' },
  { q: 'How to translate a PDF document on iPhone?', a: 'To translate a PDF on iPhone, open TranslateNow, tap the Document Translation feature, and import your PDF from Files, iCloud, or email. The app extracts all text blocks, translates each one using GPT-4o, and reconstructs the document preserving original formatting, fonts, and page layout. Supports PDF, DOCX, TXT, and photo documents with full RTL support for Arabic, Hebrew, and Urdu.' },
  { q: 'How to use voice cloning for translation?', a: 'To use voice cloning in TranslateNow, go to Settings → Voice Cloning, record a 10-second voice sample (or upload an audio file), and the ElevenLabs AI engine creates a neural clone of your voice. Once created, your cloned voice speaks all translations in 135+ languages. Adjust playback speed from 0.5x to 2x and choose male or female voice. Voice cloning requires a Pro subscription.' },
  { q: 'How to set a default translator on iPhone iOS 18.4?', a: 'To set TranslateNow as your default translator on iOS 18.4 or later, go to Settings → Apps → TranslateNow and enable the Translation provider option. Once enabled, whenever you select text in Safari, Mail, or Messages and tap "Translate" from the context menu, the translation routes through TranslateNow instead of Apple\'s built-in translator.' },
  { q: 'How to translate text offline on iPhone without internet?', a: 'To translate offline on iPhone, open TranslateNow, go to Settings → Offline Languages, and download the language packs you need (5-50 MB each). Once downloaded, translation works without any internet connection. 59 languages are available via Google ML Kit on-device translation. All processing stays on your iPhone with zero data transmitted.' },
